1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
Cinderella

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:11,030
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,980
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:23,280
Episode 5

5
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,650
I'm going to pick up Unni and go with her.

6
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:31,250
You're completely done for! Your father is very upset at you.

7
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:33,550
I said I get it.

8
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:37,250
I know..but instead of going home alone, making Unni go in front of me is better

9
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:39,830
so that's what I'm going to do.

10
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:41,800
Hang up, Uncle..

11
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:00,010
Son Sang Gi Exhibition

12
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:14,750
Why are you here?

13
00:01:17,490 --> 00:01:19,920
I came here to see the paintings.

14
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:26,280
Did you come without knowing what this was, Unni? I came here knowing about the exhibit.

15
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,730
Did you not know?

16
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:34,470
Oppa Gi Hoon told me.

17
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:38,130
What did you say?

18
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:40,030
Didn't you know?

19
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:44,860
We're dating.

20
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:49,580
Oppa Gi Hoon... and me.

21
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:59,690
Why? Do you think I'm lying?

22
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:16,030
Excuse me, was this painting in the catalog?

23
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:18,050
Yes, it was.

24
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:22,380
Really? I didn't see it.

25
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:24,360
I'll show it to you.

26
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,700
Did you not know Oppa and I were dating?

27
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,000
Maybe Oppa doesn't contact you at all..

28
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:59,150
She would want to ask me,

29
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:02,120
She would very much like to ask me,

30
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:06,180
but this annoying sister is pretending to sleep.

31
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:13,470
If she would just ask me, I could answer her in a second,

32
00:03:13,470 --> 00:03:17,230
but nothing is easy for her when it comes to me.

33
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,910
I have something to say to you, before going home..

34
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:36,660
I used my credit card so much, Father is angry. Can you calm him down for me?

35
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,690
What?

36
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:41,790
Can you help stop Dad?

37
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,210
How much did you spend?

38
00:03:45,210 --> 00:03:49,140
I don't know. Just a lot.

39
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:52,680
At the end, I couldn't use it because I exceeded the limit.

40
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,020
What were you doing that you had to spend so much money?

41
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:58,860
There are so many pretty things in this world.

42
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:05,870
You exceeded your credit buying pretty things?

43
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:08,960
I didn't just buy things for myself. I bought things for Mom and you-

44
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,320
Forget it.

45
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:14,900
I have no interest in picking up after your crazy acts.

46
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,960
Just go.

47
00:04:19,350 --> 00:04:23,890
What's so great about you that you always act like you're better than others?

48
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:27,720
I also have a thing called circumstances.

49
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:42,160
Hey..stop right there!

50
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,900
Can't you hear someone speaking to you?

51
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:55,690
- Let go of me before you speak.
- Dad is waiting with the wooden rod.

52
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:59,570
Are you going to let me get hit?

53
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:02,070
-What is your dream?
-What?

54
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:05,020
How do you plan on living the rest of your life?

55
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:08,320
Do you have anything like a strategy or plan of action?

56
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:14,040
If I have one, are you curious about even that?

57
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:17,240
Are you asking because you're curious? You're not right?!

58
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:21,540
It's another boast of yours you say when you try to step on me and it's like an introduction of what you're going to say later, right?

59
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:25,960
Your introductions when you first hear it, you don't feel anything, but when you think about it after the matter,

60
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:29,500
you feel quite horrible.

61
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,350
Did you know that?

62
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:34,650
You must know.

63
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:38,400
You're saying those things intentionally to make me feel bad. There's no reason you wouldn't know.

64
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,570
Do you want to keep doing ballet?

65
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:44,550
Of course. Do you think I'm crazy, going to auditions every day for something I don't want to do?

66
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:47,300
Then why do you get eliminated?

67
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:49,420
Why can you never pass the audition?

68
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,560
Even if you were okay, shouldn't you have passed at least one audition by now?

69
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:55,700
Hey. Do you think there are hundreds and thousands of ballet groups in our country?

70
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:57,540
Do you even practice?

71
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,000
- Do you practice until you feel you'll die?
- Of course!

72
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,350
Then why are you feet so clean and pretty?

73
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:08,900
-What?
- The toenails fall off countless times for those who practice endlessly

74
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:12,390
and their bones stick out constantly making it seem like the foot of an animal.

75
00:06:12,390 --> 00:06:17,480
Why do your feet look like feet that have never even been blistered before?

76
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:21,710
You don't practice right? You don't want to do ballet too right?

77
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:25,810
You don't have a dream, do you? You don't have a strategy or plan or action. You have no thoughts at all.

78
00:06:25,810 --> 00:06:27,660
Just say you have no thoughts.

79
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:31,470
Then I'll understand your boring life as the life of a poor kid who had nothing better to do than swipe their card,

80
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:35,520
and help you, whether that is to hide the wooden rod or break it.

81
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:39,690
Is that all you are going to say?

82
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:43,520
Don't cry in front of mel ... it's annoying.

83
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:56,980
Hyo Seon is here.

84
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:05,460
- What are you up to, you punk?
- What are you up to, you punk?

85
00:07:09,430 --> 00:07:11,300
Father!

86
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:28,860
Dad... I did wrong. I won't do it again.

87
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,610
Stand up.

88
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:34,290
Father..I said I'm sorry,

89
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:36,100
Stand up!

90
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,460
-Honey, Honey, Honey!!!

91
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:49,410
You let go of this and leave.

92
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:52,040
- Hyo Seon, hurry up and leave.
- Where are you going!

93
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,630
Hit me. I did wrong, Honey, okay?

94
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,390
Won't you move?

95
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:58,890
Hyo Seon, hurry up and leave!

96
00:07:58,890 --> 00:08:02,420
Hey! Hyo Seon! Won't you get back here?

97
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:05,330
Give this to me.

98
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:11,220
-Do you want to see me die?
- What??

99
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:13,580
Rather than see her calves bruised so purple,

100
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:16,400
I'd prefer dying.

101
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:21,180
This isn't something to cover up for her. What is she doing outside?

102
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:24,250
Hyo Seon, won't you get back here right this instant?

103
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:27,550
I'll do it. Let me do it.

104
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:30,280
Why would you hit a pretty kid that we never get to see?

105
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:35,040
If Hyo Seon's calves get bruised, I think I'll become sick.

106
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:39,780
After I gave birth to Joon Soo, when I am sick now and lie down,

107
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:43,110
I don't think I'll be able to get up.

108
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:08,820
If I get sick, would you like it?

109
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:12,840
Do you... want to become widower twice?

110
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:17,650
I'll talk to her about it.

111
00:09:17,650 --> 00:09:23,620
I've tried before, but I felt bad about her being dropped off in Seoul all by herself.

112
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:26,270
My heart hurt every time I saw her...

113
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:29,820
I told her to do whatever she wanted,

114
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:32,340
so I'm also at fault.

115
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:43,900
Even using the cards indiscriminately is a problem

116
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:48,900
but what she does. It's often she doesn't come home until its past midnight.

117
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:52,090
What did you say? After midnight?

118
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:58,100
She's older now, so it should be a given that she has a boyfriend or two,

119
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:01,500
but I feel like maybe she's meeting more than just one or two...

120
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:04,930
-What?!!
- Honey, please don't yell..

121
00:10:04,930 --> 00:10:08,790
How can a girl just be diligent all the time?

122
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:14,580
She spent a night out? More than one or two men?

123
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:17,380
Wait a minute. This little-!

124
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:20,570
If you do that, it'll seem like I snitched on her.

125
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:24,400
Don't be like that, and listen to me.

126
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:28,560
This type of talk is better if the mom does it, not the dad.

127
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:30,980
Don't you think so?

128
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:42,640
Do you think I have the right to be Hyo Seon's mother?

129
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:48,670
Is that even a question?

130
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:53,420
If you hold the wooden rod to her again,

131
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:59,330
then I'll understand it as you not acknowledging me as her mom and pack up my things.

132
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:10,250
I'll take care of it. I'll put her in place.

133
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:16,030
Let me do that, Honey.

134
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:34,220
How many tails do you have? You, Goodness ...

135
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:37,590
What do you mean, tails?

136
00:11:37,590 --> 00:11:41,010
I only have 9.

137
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:42,760
Goodness...

138
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:46,700
You little...

139
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:52,280
♫ In the solitude which wakes me up  ♫

140
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:59,120
♫ when I wake up from an exhausted sleep
♫

141
00:12:00,310 --> 00:12:04,290
Did you really not know I was dating him?

142
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:07,990
I guess he doesn't contact you at all.

143
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:13,980
♫ I'm secretly smiling ♫

144
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:22,140
♫ Love leaves again this way ♫

145
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:28,870
♫ When the beautiful season arrives ♫

146
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:37,540
♫ In the sadness you left in the longing ♫

147
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:43,130
♫ I walk this street again ♫

148
00:12:43,130 --> 00:12:50,430
♫ I am living day after day  ♫

149
00:12:50,430 --> 00:12:59,460
♫ In your name when tears appear, ah ♫

150
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,970
♫ I can't bear it ♫

151
00:13:01,970 --> 00:13:06,900
♫ So I can't laugh ♫

152
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:17,420
♫ I'll call out your name again ♫

153
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:32,190
For some reason I did think that one day

154
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:36,590
you would leave somewhere.

155
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:42,570
I know you aren't meeting Gi Hoon anymore,

156
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,360
and unfortunately,

157
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:50,730
I know neither this house nor myself

158
00:13:52,410 --> 00:13:56,390
must be great consolidation for you.

159
00:13:57,230 --> 00:14:02,810
When Gi Hoon left, I was the most worried about you.

160
00:14:05,950 --> 00:14:08,110
Let me leave.

161
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,230
I want to leave.

162
00:14:12,230 --> 00:14:14,600
I can't let you do that.

163
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:18,540
I'm going to leave.

164
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:22,170
If you don't let me leave now,

165
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:27,020
I'm going to leave on my way to school or sneak out early in the morning.

166
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,890
I'm going to leave someday.

167
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,040
I know.

168
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:44,250
When I feel like I can let you leave and not worry about you, I'll let you go.

169
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,530
I promise.

170
00:14:49,350 --> 00:14:52,820
I always keep the promises I make.

171
00:14:56,070 --> 00:15:01,590
Will you believe that I'm worried about you?

172
00:15:04,190 --> 00:15:07,070
Can you believe

173
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,200
that I will keep my promise?

174
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:19,140
For the time being, I'll be a good reason for you to stay here.

175
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:23,900
Believe me.

176
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,980
The conclusion I've reached

177
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:03,220
is that I want to pick someone.

178
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:07,760
I want to select someone who is familiar with marketing and train them until I can trust them to take care of things,

179
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:10,650
then I want to go into research.

180
00:16:10,650 --> 00:16:13,610
There's more than just one or two things you can research about on yeast.

181
00:16:13,610 --> 00:16:19,250
Do you think a young person, and a smart one at that, would come work in a countryside?

182
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:21,730
Eat up, you two.

183
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:24,600
Talk about business elsewhere.

184
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:29,890
I have no interest in making it so large.

185
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:35,210
There's a lot of things that go into just building a simple factory like this.

186
00:16:35,210 --> 00:16:38,420
- Then what will I do?
- What?

187
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:42,420
You're going to use me with no intent of growing your business?

188
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,140
How are you going to use me?

189
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:48,020
Did you have me study microbiology only to have me run errands for you?

190
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:52,620
You don't need knowledge in biochemistry to disinfect a jar.

191
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:09,150
Uh...Nothing is fun,

192
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:12,210
Who is it?

193
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,490
Mom!!

194
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:21,990
- Where is it?
- Huh?

195
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:27,150
I saw your credit card use history. It said you bought a bag. What else did you buy?

196
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:30,170
You must have every season's release!

197
00:17:30,170 --> 00:17:32,330
I bought one for you, too.

198
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:33,800
Really?

199
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:37,310
I hid it in the car in case Dad finds out.

200
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:39,550
Should I bring it right now?

201
00:17:44,290 --> 00:17:48,590
- This is for you, Mom.
- Ah!! It's so pretty!!

202
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:53,790
It's so pretty right? The moment I saw this, I thought of you.

203
00:17:53,790 --> 00:17:57,700
But, do you think I have clothes that will go with this?

204
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:00,750
Then should we go shopping for your clothes?

205
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:02,560
Shall we?

206
00:18:03,410 --> 00:18:05,970
- Let's do that.
- It's so pretty.

207
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:08,790
Are these all yours?

208
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:11,070
Wow, this one is super pretty!

209
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:13,270
It's super pretty, right?

210
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:17,690
But this one is so large that you won't look good with it.

211
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:19,190
What?

212
00:18:19,190 --> 00:18:21,140
Wait a minute..

213
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:28,400
Hey! This looks like for old people, I should use this!

214
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,120
Yes, you use it, Mom!

215
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:33,500
Right?!

216
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:37,740
We must really be mother and daughter, judging from our similar preferences.

217
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:42,810
Can you bring me the red one? And the black one next to it?

218
00:18:42,810 --> 00:18:46,760
Okay! What about the green one?

219
00:19:22,270 --> 00:19:24,250
Are you crazy?

220
00:19:24,250 --> 00:19:27,830
What am I supposed to do if you come here at night?

221
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:36,560
Hello?

222
00:19:37,870 --> 00:19:40,010
Where are you right now?

223
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:43,270
You're going to come in?

224
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:45,510
Right now, at this time of day?

225
00:20:11,530 --> 00:20:13,880
Hyo Seon, did I do something wrong?

226
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,660
If I did, tell me.

227
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:18,940
I told you that you didn't do anything wrong!

228
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:23,190
- Then why are you suddenly not picking up my calls?
- This is driving me crazy!

229
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:28,870
Hyo Seon, do you think I came here all the way from Seoul for you to act so coldly to me?

230
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:31,330
Speak to me nicely.

231
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:34,320
Okay, I'll do that.

232
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:38,500
Oppa Hyeon Gu, you should go back to Seoul today.

233
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:41,000
Drive safely, okay?

234
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,950
Oppa, why?

235
00:20:56,950 --> 00:20:59,760
What? Your tire is flat?

236
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:01,800
What does that have to do with m-

237
00:21:03,490 --> 00:21:05,960
Do you think you can get to a repair shop?

238
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:09,930
There's a new car center in that area, so go there.

239
00:21:33,770 --> 00:21:40,480
♫ Again today my memory led me astray ♫

240
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:46,060
♫ I who am strolling at the end of the street ♫

241
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:54,790
♫ where you can't hold me again ♫

242
00:21:54,790 --> 00:21:56,900
Isn't there something wrong with her sense of pain?

243
00:21:56,900 --> 00:22:00,340
♫ I ask again about the way. ♫

244
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:09,300
♫ Saying I want to see you and hold you again ♫

245
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:15,210
♫ While looking at heaven I'm praying ♫

246
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:18,710
♫ It must be you. ♫

247
00:22:18,710 --> 00:22:22,580
♫ I cannot be without you. ♫

248
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:29,550
♫ Like this for another day, month or year ♫

249
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:33,140
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt. ♫

250
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:37,130
♫ I don't mind even if my heart breaks ♫

251
00:22:37,130 --> 00:22:45,200
